From ec555c99e742b02aab9f71005faa658a0d65c76e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:55:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] setup: rename distribution to sqlcipher3-binary

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream redistribution naming, irrelevant to coleifer/sqlcipher3]

sqlcipher3-binary is a separate PyPI distribution coleifer publishes
from this same repo: a self-contained build of sqlcipher3 under a
different project name, so users can `pip install sqlcipher3-binary`
and get a wheel with no system libsqlcipher/libcrypto requirement
beyond what cibuildwheel's repair step (auditwheel) bundles in. There
is no dedicated git tag for it; every released sqlcipher3-binary
version shares its git tag with the plain sqlcipher3 release of the
same version number (confirmed: sqlcipher3-binary 0.6.0 and sqlcipher3
0.6.0 both have no sdist differences beyond this `name=` field, per
the build-scripts/_build_wheels.sh approach coleifer used before
GitHub Actions wheel builds existed). setup.py's build_ext command is
already mapped to AmalgationLibSqliteBuilder by default here (unlike
the sibling pysqlite3 repo, which needs its own such patch), so a
plain `pip wheel .` already produces the self-contained, vendored-
amalgamation build; only the distribution name needs changing.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index b15ed2b..28a064a 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -144,7 +144,7 @@ class AmalgationLibSqliteBuilder(build_ext):
 
 def get_setup_args():
     return dict(
-        name=PACKAGE_NAME,
+        name='sqlcipher3-binary',
         version=VERSION,
         description="DB-API 2.0 interface for SQLCipher 3.x",
         long_description='',
